  """The Graves runs south-east from the city of Bordeaux along the left bank of the Garonne to beyond Langon, a 50 km band of gravel, sand and clay with the Landes forest at its back. The northern section, around Pessac, Talence and Léognan, has had its own appellation, Pessac-Léognan, since 1987 and holds all the classified estates. The south wraps around the sweet-wine enclaves of Cérons, Barsac and Sauternes.""",
