  """Bordeaux Haut-Benauge is a seldom-used name, attached to AOC Bordeaux, for white wines from the Haut-Benauge, a hilly area in the south of the Entre-Deux-Mers around the castle of Benauge. The wines, dry to medium-sweet, must come from Sémillon, Sauvignon and Muscadelle; most growers in the zone prefer to sell under the better-known Entre-deux-Mers-Haut-Benauge name for dry wine.""",
