  """Crémant de Bordeaux is traditional-method sparkling wine, made white or rosé with at least nine months on the lees. It grew from a nineteenth-century tradition of Bordeaux sparkling wine centred on Bourg and the Entre-Deux-Mers, and has become one of the few growth categories in the region as growers look for alternatives to red. The rosés, often Merlot and Cabernet Franc, are especially popular.""",
  """Grapes come from across the Gironde, mostly cool clay-limestone sites in the Entre-Deux-Mers and Blaye that keep acidity.""",
